   "body": "Coordinator: assigned to macm3's free thread. 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate, raw folder `I251-macm3/`, in the worktree at 408b4d6 or on main, the two cuts one after the other:\n```\npython3 hp/modecount_circle.py hp/data/states/up6_D30.0688.npz 2.079747703853262,0,0.2 4.267,1.324,0.35 --M=64 --kf=none --fmax=1e-15 --n0=20 --tag=D30.0688_M64 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I251-macm3/nocut > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I251-macm3/circles_nocut.log 2>&1\npython3 hp/modecount_circle.py hp/data/states/up6_D30.0688.npz 2.079747703853262,0,0.2 4.267,1.324,0.35 --M=64 --kf=13 --fmax=1e-15 --n0=20 --tag=D30.0688_M64_kf13 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I251-macm3/kf13 > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I251-macm3/circles_kf13.log 2>&1\n```\nThe setup fits the layout itself (a node at 0.15 where the centre series needs it, #141) and takes about 15 minutes. If it refuses the layout or misses the 1e-15 gate, report it and stop that cut.\n\n**Reading, written before the runs:** the \u03bb_phys circle is the control and must wind +1. Report its miss from 2.079747703853262 with the circle's own estimate; a miss up to 1e-3 does not stop the run, since M 64 determinants are known to be noisy (#252). The circle at 4.267 + 1.324i, where October's M 48 count on the old layout had its extra pair, winds 0 (no zero there at M 64) or +1 (the pair exists at M 64).\n",
